          "id": "v2-proposal-j2-131911-j2-gp-a",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "In how many orders can 2 successes and 6 failures occur in 8 trials?",
          "answerSpaceMm": 40,
          "answer": {
           "short": "$21$",
           "worked": "Write the 6 failures first:\n\n$$\\_\\;F\\;\\_\\;F\\;\\_\\;F\\;\\_\\;F\\;\\_\\;F\\;\\_\\;F\\;\\_$$\n\nThis creates 7 gaps. Choose 2 of them for the successes.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}N&=\\binom{7}{2}\\\\&=21\\end{aligned}$$"
          }
         },
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j2-131911-j2-gp-b",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "In how many orders can 4 successes and 5 failures occur in 9 trials?",
          "answerSpaceMm": 40,
          "answer": {
           "short": "$15$",
           "worked": "Write the 5 failures first:\n\n$$\\_\\;F\\;\\_\\;F\\;\\_\\;F\\;\\_\\;F\\;\\_\\;F\\;\\_$$\n\nThis creates 6 gaps. Choose 4 of them for the successes.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}N&=\\binom{6}{4}\\\\&=15\\end{aligned}$$"
          }
         },
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j2-131911-j2-gp-c",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "There are 10 chairs in a row. How many ways are there to paint 4 of them red, if no two red chairs are adjacent?",
          "answerSpaceMm": 40,
          "answer": {
           "short": "$35$",
           "worked": "The 4 red chairs are the successes and the 6 unpainted chairs are the failures.\n\nWrite the 6 unpainted chairs first. This creates 7 gaps. Choose 4 of them for the red chairs.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}N&=\\binom{7}{4}\\\\&=35\\end{aligned}$$"
          }
         }
        ]
