     "replacement": "A **Bernoulli distribution** shows the probability of ‘success’ and ‘failure’.\n\nCalculate the expected value, variance and standard deviation using the same formulas as for any discrete random variable.\n\n**Expected value**\n\n$$E(X)=\\sum xP(x)$$\n**Variance & standard deviation**\n\n$$\\operatorname{Var}(X)=\\left[\\sum x^2P(x)\\right]-E(X)^2$$\n\n$$\\sigma(X)=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{Var}(X)}$$",
